.\logs\codex-20261028T0050330184002Z-083ce22b36a74990a69855563700d944.log:1541:logs\codex-20261027T1622194980844Z-de0ba5c888594b398a77c6585792e4a0.log:240:"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command '$paths = @('"'C:\\AGENTS.md','C:\\Users\\AGENTS.md','C:\\Users\\ovisa\\AGENTS.md','C:\\Users\\ovisa\\Documents\\AGENTS.md','C:\\Users\\ovisa\\Documents\\OAF_App\\AGENTS.md','C:\\Users\\ovisa\\Documents\\OAF_App\\Development\\AGENTS.md','C:\\Users\\ovisa\\Documents\\OAF_App\\Development\\OAF Website\\AGENTS.md'); foreach ("'$p in $paths) { if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $p) { Write-Output "FILE: $p"; Get-Content -LiteralPath $p } }; Get-Content -LiteralPath docs/WORKFLOW.md; rg -n --hidden -g '"'"'!node_modules'"' -g '"'!.git'"' -g '"'!.venv'"' -g '"'!*.xml'"' -g '"'!*.json'"' 'Invoke-OAFCodex|clipboard|read-back|completion alert|WU2' ops docs .vscode .pytest_cache/wu2-web-20261027T044519Z-2080d85d logs" in C:\Users\ovisa\Documents\OAF_App\Development\OAF Website
.\logs\codex-20261028T0050330184002Z-083ce22b36a74990a69855563700d944.log:1549:logs\codex-20261027T1622194980844Z-de0ba5c888594b398a77c6585792e4a0.log:483:- **Policy C - authorization:** Require a distinct, deliberate owner-issued record with a unique UUID, UTC issuance and expiry, and lifetime of at most 24 hours. Bind the exact environment, operation, expected starting state, target revision, independently approved manifest/revision hashes, applicable prerequisite approvals, and predecessor claim. Reject missing, malformed, future-dated, expired, reused, mismatched, or stale records. Revalidate the exact bound authorization UUID, bytes, and UTC validity at the final runner and Alembic pre-mutation boundaries and immediately before commit, after required audit persistence. Matching hashes prove integrity only. The runner consumes records and never issues or approves them. Issuance is separate from artifact approval, and neither authorizes another environment or a later no-op.
.\logs\codex-20261028T0050330184002Z-083ce22b36a74990a69855563700d944.log:1550:logs\codex-20261027T1622194980844Z-de0ba5c888594b398a77c6585792e4a0.log:494:The minimal issuer reads a UTF-8 JSON specification with exactly four keys: `request`, `artifact_approval`, `prerequisite_approval`, and `expires_utc`. `request` has exactly `action` (`verify` or `upgrade`), `environment`, `expected_start`, `target`, `manifest_hash`, and `revision_hash`. Both approval references have exactly `id` (canonical UUID) and `sha256` (SHA-256 of the approval file's exact bytes). `expires_utc` must be UTC, later than issuance, and no more than 24 hours later. Manifest/framework/revision hashes retain the existing `sha256-utf8-lf` normalization; approval-file and predecessor-claim hashes use exact bytes.
.\logs\codex-20261028T0050330184002Z-083ce22b36a74990a69855563700d944.log:1552:logs\codex-20261027T1622194980844Z-de0ba5c888594b398a77c6585792e4a0.log:499:- `prerequisite-approval-<uuid>.json`: the same six common fields, with `kind=prerequisite_approval`, plus `environment`, `expected_start`, `approvals`, `predecessor`, `owner_reconciliation`, and `testing_validation_run`. `approvals` maps exactly `dependency_acceptance`, `bootstrap_validation`, `lock_and_timeouts`, `search_path_and_postconditions`, `recovery_procedure`, and `audit_policies` to UUID references to applicable reviewed approvals. These are explicit local attestations of those reviews, not automated proof of their substantive correctness. For testing, `testing_validation_run` is null; for development, it references a completed successful testing `upgrade` run with matching artifact hashes: either acknowledged commit with verified postconditions or a fully verified target no-op. Require published terminal completion bound to that run, authorization, claim, and exact acknowledged event bytes. A partial or success-looking terminal record never qualifies. After an exceptional testing outcome, the existing owner reconciliation prerequisite must bind the exact testing predecessor and verified DB state, followed by a fresh separately authorized testing operation and completed target validation. Reconciliation alone never rewrites a failed result or substitutes for testing validation or independent artifact approval.
.\logs\codex-20261028T0050330184002Z-083ce22b36a74990a69855563700d944.log:1553:logs\codex-20261027T1622194980844Z-de0ba5c888594b398a77c6585792e4a0.log:510:Deterministic autonomy review: environment/request selection, approval/hash binding, UTC expiry, claim competition, denial persistence, audit transitions, transaction/commit classification, no-op checks, and recovery blocking use fixed rules without AI. Independent review, deliberate owner issuance, prerequisite attestation, and exceptional reconciliation remain the approved administrative boundaries. Offline success proves tested source behavior only; live PostgreSQL semantics, operational validation, independent artifact approval, and a later testing-only execution authorization remain separate gates.
