.\logs\codex-20261028T0050330184002Z-083ce22b36a74990a69855563700d944.log:2866:logs\codex-20261028T0044337148261Z-e67ee9f4ea9c4e89a0db4aaf7b10f2d7.log:1377:- `prerequisite-approval-<uuid>.json`: the same six common fields, with `kind=prerequisite_approval`, plus `environment`, `expected_start`, `approvals`, `predecessor`, `owner_reconciliation`, and `testing_validation_run`. `approvals` maps exactly `dependency_acceptance`, `bootstrap_validation`, `lock_and_timeouts`, `search_path_and_postconditions`, `recovery_procedure`, and `audit_policies` to UUID references to applicable reviewed approvals. These are explicit local attestations of those reviews, not automated proof of their substantive correctness. For testing, `testing_validation_run` is null; for development, it references a completed successful testing `upgrade` run with matching artifact hashes: either acknowledged commit with verified postconditions or a fully verified target no-op. Require published terminal completion bound to that run, authorization, claim, and exact acknowledged event bytes. A partial or success-looking terminal record never qualifies. After an exceptional testing outcome, the existing owner reconciliation prerequisite must bind the exact testing predecessor and verified DB state, followed by a fresh separately authorized testing operation and completed target validation. Reconciliation alone never rewrites a failed result or substitutes for testing validation or independent artifact approval.
.\logs\codex-20261028T0050330184002Z-083ce22b36a74990a69855563700d944.log:2867:logs\codex-20261028T0044337148261Z-e67ee9f4ea9c4e89a0db4aaf7b10f2d7.log:1388:Deterministic autonomy review: environment/request selection, approval/hash binding, UTC expiry, claim competition, denial persistence, audit transitions, transaction/commit classification, no-op checks, and recovery blocking use fixed rules without AI. Independent review, deliberate owner issuance, prerequisite attestation, and exceptional reconciliation remain the approved administrative boundaries. Offline success proves tested source behavior only; live PostgreSQL semantics, operational validation, independent artifact approval, and a later testing-only execution authorization remain separate gates.
.\logs\codex-20261028T0050330184002Z-083ce22b36a74990a69855563700d944.log:2869:logs\codex-20261028T0044337148261Z-e67ee9f4ea9c4e89a0db4aaf7b10f2d7.log:4910:## WU3 - OAF state availability source and focused offline validation (2026-10-27)
